english_question:
The straight line given in the figure $\mathtt{y}=\mathtt{k}_{1}\mathtt{x}+\mathtt{b}$ and the hyperbolic function $\mathrm{y}=\frac{\mathrm{k}_{2}}{\mathrm{x}}$, determine how many of the following conclusions are correct: ( ) 
1. $\mathtt{k}_{2}>\mathtt{b}>\mathtt{k}_{1}>0$ ; 
2. The area of triangle ABO formed by the line $y=k_{1}x+b$ and the coordinate axes is 4; 
3. The solution of the system of equations $\begin{array}{l}{\left\{{\mathrm{y}}={\mathrm{k}}_{1}{\mathrm{x}}+{\mathrm{b}}\right.}\\ {\left.{\mathrm{y}}=\frac{{\mathrm{k}}_{2}}{\mathrm{x}}\right.}\end{array}$ is $\begin{array}{r}{\left\{\mathrm{x}_{1}=-6\,\mathrm{\Delta}\right\}\mathrm{x}_{2}=2}\\ {\left\{\mathrm{y}_{1}=-1\,^{\prime}\right\}\mathrm{y}_{2}=3}\end{array}$ ; 
4. When $-6<x<2$, $\mathtt{k_{1}x+b}>\frac{\mathtt{k}_{2}}{\mathtt{x}}$.
A. 1
B. 2
C. 3
D. 4

In the figure, the median \(AF\) of the equilateral triangle \(ABC\) with side length \(a\) intersects the midline \(DE\) at point \(G\). It is known that \(\triangle A'DE (A' \notin \text{plane } ABC)\) is a figure during the rotation process of \(\triangle ADE\) around \(DE\). The following statements are given: 
\(①\) Plane \(A'FG \perp \) plane \(ABC\); 
\(② BC \parallel \) plane \(A'DE\); 
\(③\) The maximum volume of the triangular pyramid \(A'-DEF\) is \( \dfrac {1}{64}a^{3}\); 
\(④\) The projection of point \(A'\) on plane \(ABC\) lies on segment \(AF\); 
\(⑤\) The range of the dihedral angle \(A'-DE-F\) is \([0, \dfrac {\pi}{2}].\) 
Which of the statements are correct? (Write down the numbers of all correct statements)
